#: includes/class-privacy.php:342
msgid "Who runs this site."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: provider of the service, with its identification.
#: includes/class-privacy.php:344
#, php-format
msgid "%s provides this service free of charge to parishes and prayer groups to manage their prayer requests. It acts as data processor (art. 28 of the GDPR): it processes the data only on behalf of and on the instructions of each controller, and never for purposes of its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:345
#: includes/class-privacy.php:347
msgid "Who is responsible."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:346
msgid "The controller of each prayer request, and of the data of the members of each group, is the parish or body shown on the form of that group, with its contact for data protection."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: data controller (a parish, an association…).
#: includes/class-privacy.php:349
#, php-format
msgid "%s is responsible for the prayer requests sent through this site and for the data of the members of its prayer groups."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: email or address for data protection.
#: includes/class-privacy.php:351
#, php-format
msgid "You can write to %s about your data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:354
msgid "You can access your data, rectify it, erase it, restrict or object to its processing, ask for its portability and withdraw your consent at any time, before the controller of your group (in the contact shown on its form) or writing to the provider of the service, who will pass your request on to it. You can also complain to the data protection supervisory authority (in Spain, the Agencia Española de Protección de Datos)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:355
msgid "You can access your data, rectify it, erase it, restrict or object to its processing, ask for its portability and withdraw your consent at any time, writing to the contact above or with the contact or phone you gave in the form. You can also complain to the data protection supervisory authority (in Spain, the Agencia Española de Protección de Datos)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:361
msgid "What data we collect."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:362
msgid "When you send a prayer request we collect your name, a way to contact you if you give it (email or phone), the name of the person you ask us to pray for, your relationship with them, the text of your intention, the dates you give and how the names may appear. It may include data about health or religious beliefs, which are special categories of personal data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:363
msgid "Purpose and legal basis."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:364
msgid "We use these data only to pray for your intention in the group you write to and, if you left a contact, to ask you how it goes. The legal basis is your explicit consent (arts. 6.1.a and 9.2.a of the GDPR)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:365
msgid "Who sees them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:366
msgid "Only the leaders of the group read your request: in their private panel, in their app and, if the group keeps it so, in an email notice. A leader may also use a program of their own (a routine) that works on the group's list with a password only for this, from their own computer. The group receives a short summary written by the leaders, with the names only as you chose (full name, first name, initials or anonymous), through its messaging channel. The full text is never shared with the group."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:367
msgid "Services that take part."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:368
msgid "The summaries reach the group through messaging services such as WhatsApp or Telegram, and the notices for the leaders by email and, if configured, by Telegram or a webhook. If the form uses Cloudflare Turnstile against abuse, Cloudflare receives your IP address. Some of these services may process data outside the European Union, under the safeguards each of them offers, such as the EU–US Data Privacy Framework or standard contractual clauses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:369
msgid "The provider of the service relies on these subprocessors:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:370
msgid "How long we keep them."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of days.
#: includes/class-privacy.php:372
#, php-format
msgid "While we pray for your intention and until the leaders close it; then it is deleted, with its updates and notes, %d days later. To stop abuse, your IP address is kept only as a one-way hash for one hour, and what you typed is kept for a few minutes if the form has to be shown again after an error."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:373
msgid "People we pray for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:374
msgid "When you ask for someone else, we do not inform them directly, because it would be impossible or would require a disproportionate effort (art. 14.5.b of the GDPR). To protect them, the group only receives a discreet summary without diagnoses, with their name as you chose, and they can exercise the same rights as you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:375
msgid "Members of the group."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:376
msgid "For the members of each group the leaders keep their name, how they are called, their phone, their birthday, the date of their death and short notes, to name them correctly and to remember their birthdays and the anniversaries of their death in the daily message. The legal basis is the legitimate interest of the group and, as members of a religious body, art. 9.2.d of the GDPR: these data are not disclosed outside it without their consent. They are kept while they belong to the group, and any member can ask to see them or to have them erased."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:377
msgid "Invitations to lead a group."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of days.
#: includes/class-privacy.php:379
#, php-format
msgid "A leader of a group may invite another person to lead it, with their name and email: they receive an email with a link to accept, valid for %1$d days. The invitation is kept until it is accepted or expires (at most %1$d days) and is deleted when it expires, or a week after it is accepted. Whoever accepts it gets an account on this site as a leader of that group, and the administrator of the site is told."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:380
msgid "Minors."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: minimum age.
#: includes/class-privacy.php:382
#, php-format
msgid "You must be at least %d years old to send a request on your own."
msgstr ""

